Rubinstein <picommander@t-online.de> writes:
> It happened 2 times in my current game: I was zapped by a monster's wand
> which turned out to be an old one, dropped by myself after fully
> identified (0:0) and named as empty. I don't believe in the incredible
> luck for the 2 monsters both having wrenched out the very last blow out of
> their wand. Looks like a bug, doesn't it?

It certainly would be, were it to occur; however, since there's code
specifically to prevent this, I suggest that something else was
happening. Each of find_offensive(), find_defensive(), and
find_misc() carefully checks for obj->spe > 0 before allowing a
monster to select a wand as an item to use. (Monsters are assumed to
know when wands are empty, identified or not; this is an arbitrary
assumption, and commented as such.)

